# caught-looking

- **Start here**: **`AGENTS.md`** — install/configure/run/test commands, constraints (paths to avoid), and definition of done, shared with Claude Code and any other agent. This rule stays as the Cursor-native always-apply entry point; keep the two in sync in spirit, don't duplicate long content here.
- **Stack**: Go 1.26 API (`backend/`, chi), React 19 + Vite + TypeScript 6 (`frontend/`).
- **Local dev**: from repo root, `make dev` runs the API (:8080) and Vite; the frontend proxies `/api` to the backend (see `Makefile`).
- **Scoped rules**: follow the matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` when editing frontend TSX/hooks, API client/types, OpenAPI, tests, backend Go, **`README.md`**, or stack manifests (`frontend/package.json`, `backend/go.mod`, CI workflow — see **`readme`** rule). Frontend Prettier: **`frontend-prettier`** (run Prettier on changed files). Editor format-on-save: **`.vscode/settings.json`**.
- **Workflow skills** (read `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` when the task fits):
  - **`openapi-maintain`** / **`add-api-endpoint`** — API contract and new routes
  - **`backend-go-tests`** / **`frontend-vitest-tests`** — tests
  - **`backend-http-security`** / **`caching-and-upstream-perf`** — hardening and upstream/cache performance
  - **`pr-ready`** — local CI-parity checks before a PR
  - **`pr-summary-draft`** — why-first PR Summary from the real diff (complements path-based PR guide scaffolding)
  - **`doc-sync-patch`** — patch README/project-stack.mdc/AGENTS.md version drift after a dependency bump
  - **`dependabot-triage`** — classify open Dependabot PR risk from changelog + required CI; merge only PRs the user names
  - **`adr-doc-sync-check`** — flag TTL/QPS/CORS/security-header/OpenAPI-workflow changes missing a matching ADR or threat-model update
  - **`coverage-gap-diagnosis`** — name the specific untested branches in changed files, not just a coverage percentage
  - **`venue-data-sync`** — check `mlbVenueFieldDimensions.ts` against the live MLB API after a team relocation or new ballpark
- **Durable rationale** (update with matching skills when decisions change): **`docs/adr/`** (cache TTLs, QPS, OpenAPI), **`docs/threat-model.md`**
- **Agent definition of done**:
  - **Task done**: follow scoped rules/skills for files you touched; ensure frontend edits are Prettier-clean (`.cursor/hooks/prettier-frontend.sh` on `afterFileEdit`, plus **`frontend-prettier`**); run the **smallest** relevant check (focused package tests, `make check-openapi` if the API contract changed). Do **not** require full CI for every small edit.
  - **PR done**: run **`make ci-local`** and follow **`.cursor/skills/pr-ready/SKILL.md`** (PR template; no secrets). Commit, push, or open a PR **only when the user asks**. After merge, delete local feature branches when cleaning up (see **`pr-ready`**).
- **Before opening a PR**: **`make ci-local`** (see **`pr-ready`**). Fill out `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
